[6.206, "o", "Commit: `3063993a` — **\"perf(v4): cut per-schema memory ~90% by moving methods to the prototype (#6318)\"**\r\n\r\nSchemas carried their methods as own properties, pushing instances past V8's inline-slot limit (~12 props = 128 B; ≥21 = 1616 B). Moving methods to the prototype fixed it:\r\n\r\n- `z.string()` retained size 7709 → 816 B; a 500-schema catalogue 198 MB → 62.7 MB\r\n- construction 45–83% faster (parse unchanged)\r\n- bundle +~150–200 B gzipped — the one axis that regressed\r\n\r\nVerified via `git show 3063993a`: the diff relocates methods to per-constructor prototypes and rewrites `$constructor` in `packages/zod/src/v4/core/core.ts` to bind proto methods per instance on first access, reusing a shared descriptor and releasing the `deferred` list after init. The follow-up `b1077f05` (#6415) continued the same theme, moving lazily-derived `_zod` internals onto a per-constructor prototype.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.184, "x", "0"]
